"### Cash-Flow Read \u2014 Hyperliquid as a cash-flowing asset\n\n**HYPE $79.04** \u00b7 mkt cap **$17.58B** \u00b7 FDV **$75.51B** \u00b7 30d -3.4% \u00b7 1y +124.8%\n\nHyperliquid earned **$908.82M of fees** over the trailing year (**$1.07B** annualising the last 30 days), of which **$691.42M is protocol revenue** (**76% margin** \u2014 the rest leaks to HLP market-makers & deployers). All-time fees: **$1.67B**.\n\nNearly all protocol revenue funds the **Assistance Fund buyback/burn**. At the current run-rate that is \u2248 **$691.42M/yr** of HYPE bought & burned \u2014 a **3.9% buyback yield** on market cap (**0.9%** on FDV). At $79.04 that retires \u2248 **8.7M HYPE/yr**, vs. rough scheduled team unlocks of \u2248 **79M/yr** (insiders have historically released *below* schedule).\n\nThat prices HYPE at **a moderately-priced ~25\u00d7 trailing revenue** (P/S **19\u00d7** on fees; **~20\u00d7** on the 30-day-annualised run-rate). Fully-diluted, 4.3\u00d7 more supply exists than circulates today \u2014 the dilution the burn has to out-run.\n\n<sub>Live: **$2.08B** 24h perp volume across **234** markets (**1** RWA/TradFi), **$11.20B** open interest, blended take **~15.11 bps**. Buyback = DefiLlama-revenue proxy; exact on-chain burn (0xfefe\u2026fefe) is a v2 upgrade. Not investment advice.</sub>"